course: dictionary
lesson: 9816
title: Clothes words and where you are
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can name the same thing in different places. In the USA and Canada, people often say «sweater» for a warm top that covers your body and your arms.
explain: «A sweater, a coat, a shirt with long sleeves — each has 2 sleeves, one for each arm.» The sentence gives you a clue: a sweater has sleeves, so it covers your arms too. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
explain: In the UK and Ireland, people often say «jumper» for the same kind of clothing. In Australia and New Zealand you may hear «jumper» or «jersey». When you read a story, the place and the words around the clothing can tell you which word the writer means.
fact: A sweater is a warm piece of clothing, often knitted from wool, that covers the top half of your body and your arms.
fact: «Put on a sweater» means to dress yourself in one, especially when it is cold.
fact: «A wool sweater» is a sweater made from wool.
fact: The word «sweater» is common in the USA and Canada, while «jumper» is common in the UK and Ireland.
fact: A sweater can also mean a person who sweats a lot, but this meaning is rare.
exercise: «A sweater, a coat, a shirt with long sleeves — each has 2 sleeves.» How many sleeves does a sweater have? | *Two | One | Three | Four
exercise: In the UK, many people call a sweater a what? | *Jumper | Scarf | Sock | Blazer
exercise: «Put on a sweater» means what? | Knit a new scarf from wool | Take off a warm top and throw it away | *Dress yourself in a warm top | Wash your hair in a sink
test: What does «a wool sweater» mean? | A sweater that is very old | A sweater for the beach | A sweater with a hood | *A sweater made from wool
test: Which country might use the word «jersey» for a warm top? | Scotland | Germany | *Australia | Canada
exam: Which word means about the same as «sweater» for someone in the UK? | Glove | *Jumper | Shirt | Coat
